{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons","id":1089031,"title":"Tuatha/Fomorians and other Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T00:33:13-07:00","id":1089031,"title":"Tuatha/Fomorians and other Pantheons","content":"So while I do like the Tuatha and Fomorians as the default Changeling names for the Old Fae, I also really like slight references to other myths, like Aesin being themed after Aesir, perhaps with slight Vanir hints. Its kind of wishy washy, because they have things like Changeling Padshah's that are part of a Welsh house, so okay so the Noble houses are Universal. But wait... the Nunnehi don't acknowledge them... oh wait Neither do the Hsien...<br /> <br /> So its kind of weird having one of the Thallain be Polynesian but keep on referencing being of the Fomorians.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the Tuatha Fomorian divide just became the prominent Zeitgeist of the Dreaming after the Sundering. While some Sidhe are Sidhe but are actually reflecting Hellenic Nymphs, and Indian Apsaras (Well Apsaras would probably also work as a separate kith but you get the idea)...<br /> <br /> So Tuatha is just shorthand for old Dream God, and Fomorian is shorthand for Primordial Nightmare God. So I would indeed like a Tuatha reflecting being a Vanir, and a Fomorian reflecting a Jotun. I remember in Shadownessence someone was doing a cool project on Fomorians and they had their Colored Courts but also Titans, and Jotun.<br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts on this?<br /> <br /> And was the War of Trees before mankind? Were the Fianna a Tribe back then?<br /> <br /> And What is the difference between a Denizen and being a Tuatha/Fomorian? Is it because Denizens are unaligned, or is it because they are a power league below them? Would Dark Age Fae become Denizens/Changelings while Gods become Tuatha/Fomorians? So True Fae being different then Tuatha, by True Fae being predecessors to Changelings, and the Tuatha/Fomorians being predecessors to the True Fae? Or are True Fae and Tuatha interchangeable?<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of Exalted so I like the Idea of Fomorians being Raksha, while Tuatha are just Raksha that choose Creation over Rakshastan, and Hsien being Descendants of Raksha that somehow agreed to serve Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:21:55-07:00","id":1089054,"title":"","content":"Yes, it was Lords of Nightmare. There is a Facebook group for it still. A few of us tried to revive it a year or so ago, but things stalled until now. I mainly did a bit of editing on the already-written material. It was really good. Made the Fomorians playable.<br /> <br /> In light of C20, they'd probably need one or more Nightmare Legacies. Probably two. Although, since Bedlam and Nightmare are now directly linked, it'll have to consider Bedlam too--making it a kind of Book of Madness for Changeling.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm not sure Nightmare should lead to Bedlam. Bedlam should be every bit as much a part of the Tuathan Dream as it is the Fomorian Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:27:23-07:00","id":1089056,"title":"","content":"I thought, that Nightmare as a Trait doesn't mean the same, as Nightmare as, well, 'nightmare' - either as a type of dream or region of Dreaming and core theme of chimeric creature or kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T04:38:35-07:00","id":1089074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089056#post1089056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought, that Nightmare as a Trait doesn't mean the same, as Nightmare as, well, 'nightmare' - either as a type of dream or region of Dreaming and core theme of chimeric creature or kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the name is confusing. But I think it is supposed to be the same thing, since Thallain have Nightmare Legacies too. Nightmare seems equivalent to both Bedlam AND the Fomorian Dream now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:31:18-07:00","id":1089082,"title":"","content":"Which would be weird.<br /> <br /> Too much of a Dreaming = Bad<br /> Too much of Dreaming/Wild Magic &gt;&gt;&gt; Nightmare<br /> Too much of a Nightmare &gt;&gt;&gt; Bedlam<br /> Also, Nightmare = Fomorian<br /> <br /> Undoing (Banality) is opposite to Bedlam (Glamour)<br /> <br /> Ergo to fight off Fomorian Dream &gt;&gt;&gt; Embrace Banality(???)<br /> <br /> Banality = Thuathan Dream(???)<br /> <br /> Resisting Banality = defying the will of Thuatha de Dannan(?????)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-07-2017, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:35:36-07:00","id":1089101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons#post1089031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I do like the Tuatha and Fomorians as the default Changeling names for the Old Fae, I also really like slight references to other myths, like Aesin being themed after Aesir, perhaps with slight Vanir hints. Its kind of wishy washy, because they have things like Changeling Padshah's that are part of a Welsh house, so okay so the Noble houses are Universal. But wait... the Nunnehi don't acknowledge them... oh wait Neither do the Hsien...<br /> <br /> So its kind of weird having one of the Thallain be Polynesian but keep on referencing being of the Fomorians.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the Tuatha Fomorian divide just became the prominent Zeitgeist of the Dreaming after the Sundering. While some Sidhe are Sidhe but are actually reflecting Hellenic Nymphs, and Indian Apsaras (Well Apsaras would probably also work as a separate kith but you get the idea)...<br /> <br /> So Tuatha is just shorthand for old Dream God, and Fomorian is shorthand for Primordial Nightmare God. So I would indeed like a Tuatha reflecting being a Vanir, and a Fomorian reflecting a Jotun. I remember in Shadownessence someone was doing a cool project on Fomorians and they had their Colored Courts but also Titans, and Jotun.<br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts on this?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tuatha and Fomorians make sense with most indo-european fae, but not with some other cultures, so I prefer to look at it on a case by case basis. It's often awkard to treat the celtic paradigm as universal when there are Trolls and Satyrs running around, so shifting the perspective to have the Fomorians be Jotnar and Titans by another name is a nice touch, but when it come to fae from cultures that don't have a race of antaonistic evil gods, it's just weird.<br /> I guess the Eshu could see the Fomorians as Rakshasas, Asuras or Daevas, since they have Indian and Persian as well as African roots?<br /> I don't know enough about Polynesian and Native American folklore to know what the Menehune and Nunnehi could equate the Fomorians to, though, but I've not read or heard of anything close to the concept, so it's perhaps just as well that it's not forced on them.<br /> Hsien are another thing entirely, and I really wonder what they even do in a Changeling book. I really hoped they would be brought more in touch with the Dreaming for this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:38:02-07:00","id":1089103,"title":"","content":"It is weird. Unintended, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:01:13-07:00","id":1089157,"title":"","content":"Most cultures have an Elder Gods, or a Those That Came Before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:27:08-07:00","id":1089169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089082#post1089082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would be weird.<br /> <br /> Too much of a Dreaming = Bad<br /> Too much of Dreaming/Wild Magic &gt;&gt;&gt; Nightmare<br /> Too much of a Nightmare &gt;&gt;&gt; Bedlam<br /> Also, Nightmare = Fomorian<br /> <br /> Undoing (Banality) is opposite to Bedlam (Glamour)<br /> <br /> Ergo to fight off Fomorian Dream &gt;&gt;&gt; Embrace Banality(???)<br /> <br /> Banality = Thuathan Dream(???)<br /> <br /> Resisting Banality = defying the will of Thuatha de Dannan(?????)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, if both Nightmare are the same, it just means that Fomorian are like the extreme Dreaming and Tuatha de Danaan are more a balanced Dreaming or perhaps more serene. The Banality, in the other hand, is the antithesis of the Dreaming, so it makes sense it could help temper the bad manifestation of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> In fact, it makes some kind of sense if Bedlam and Fomorian are related. Because both are about madness... but not necessarily the same kind of madness though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:34:05-07:00","id":1089175,"title":"","content":"I can only speak for myself as a writer. Not the rest of the team, not the line as a whole. <br /> <br /> I used &quot;nightmare&quot;, &quot;nightmare realm&quot; and &quot;nightmare trods&quot; frequently to describe the darker aspects of the Dreaming and Glamour. Think like, Poe or Lovecraft darker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:37:14-07:00","id":1089177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089157#post1089157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most cultures have an Elder Gods, or a Those That Came Before.</div> </div> </div> </div>With respect, I doubt anyone has counted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:09:51-07:00","id":1089201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089177#post1089177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With respect, I doubt anyone has counted.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a contrary, most probably some geeky scientist already counted. The problem is to quickly find out who. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:21:21-07:00","id":1089241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089157#post1089157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most cultures have an Elder Gods, or a Those That Came Before.</div> </div> </div> </div>i was under the impression that the fomorians weren't exactly the fomorians of irish history,but a catcha ll term for all of the Elder gods. and tuatha are a term for more . So in the mythic ages there were Polynesian,Chinese and African &quot;Tuatha&quot; and &quot;fomorians&quot;,did i understand it correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:41:36-07:00","id":1089256,"title":"","content":"That's my take on it, but it's admittedly difficult to reconcile with, say, the hsien who have nothing to do with anything involving the Kithain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:49:26-07:00","id":1089261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089256#post1089256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my take on it, but it's admittedly difficult to reconcile with, say, the hsien who have nothing to do with anything involving the Kithain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The explanation could be that the Hsien like all fae also had primordial ancestors,who weren't tuatha,but had somo similiarities with the ancestors of the kithain. It could be that different areas of the dreaming acrssthe world each had their rulers and their fae beings that would eventually become changelings,all different but all born from the dreaming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:18:13-07:00","id":1089269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089261#post1089261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The explanation could be that the Hsien like all fae also had primordial ancestors,who weren't tuatha,but had somo similiarities with the ancestors of the kithain. It could be that different areas of the dreaming acrssthe world each had their rulers and their fae beings that would eventually become changelings,all different but all born from the dreaming</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the Hsien don't make sense. Even they don't understand why the Fae think they're related. They have no link to the Dreaming, and have their own cosmology. As they are, they're closer to the Kuei-jin than to Changelings.<br /> I hope they get re-written as being part of the Dreaming in a later book. Still nice to see them, though. They're nice to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:34:42-07:00","id":1089276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089269#post1089269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, the Hsien don't make sense. Even they don't understand why the Fae think they're related. They have no link to the Dreaming, and have their own cosmology. As they are, they're closer to the Kuei-jin than to Changelings.<br /> I hope they get re-written as being part of the Dreaming in a later book. Still nice to see them, though. They're nice to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>ooh i didnt know that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:59:59-07:00","id":1089295,"title":"","content":"I find the hsien to be disappointing, actually. Apparently Asian people don't dream and have zero effect on the Dreaming. Or have folktales or mythologies or tale tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:41:38-07:00","id":1089316,"title":"","content":"The Hsien seem to be closest to Demon the Fallen really. But they fit with the Dark Age Fae but not Changeling. But they do kinda seem similar to Nunnehi. It's like not all Fae aspects to the Dreaming after the Shattering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:12:14-07:00","id":1089335,"title":"","content":"Titanomachies are more prevalent in Indo-European religions and mythologies, I believe, but there may be some similar precursor god myths too. So there are the Asuras in Indian culture, Ahuras in Persian culture, Jotun in Norse and the Ilani Kamuti in Mesopotamia. Similar myths include the Ogdoad/Khemenu in Ancient Egypt, which aren't identical, but might make for a Fomorian analogue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:19:21-07:00","id":1089338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089335#post1089335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Titanomachies are more prevalent in Indo-European religions and mythologies, I believe, but there may be some similar precursor god myths too. So there are the Asuras in Indian culture, Ahuras in Persian culture, Jotun in Norse and the Ilani Kamuti in Mesopotamia. Similar myths include the Ogdoad/Khemenu in Ancient Egypt, which aren't identical, but might make for a Fomorian analogue.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ogdoad were primordial gods, but not antagonistic as far as I know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:53:55-07:00","id":1089437,"title":"","content":"The egyptian equivalent for the Fomorian, would be Apep, I guess? At least, Apep is an analogue for Tiamat in some extent (incarnation of primordial chaos water), which could be related to the Fomorian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:38:35-07:00","id":1089627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089437#post1089437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The egyptian equivalent for the Fomorian, would be Apep, I guess? At least, Apep is an analogue for Tiamat in some extent (incarnation of primordial chaos water), which could be related to the Fomorian.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Apep is already tied to a More Neverborn Angle, in my headcanon Apep is the Arse End of the Wyrm, the Head that represent Oblivion.<br /> <br /> But Fomorians in Changeling not just represent precursors to the gods but also Prehuman Dreams, so I can see some some Primordial gods perceived by Humans as Benign being Fomorians, perhaps ones that don't go out of their way to eat people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:40:57-07:00","id":1089629,"title":"","content":"Also I am reminded of the Classic Gargoyles Series, were the King of Faeries is also the King of the Gods. So Oberon and before him Queen Mab his mother were the Lord that Gods such as Anubis and Odin would kneel too.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which did we ever get mention of Oberon or Queen Mab in Changeling? I think I recall mention of Queen Mab somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:34:06-07:00","id":1089665,"title":"","content":"Queen Maab is the ruler of the Kingdom of Apple, if I recall correctly but no, I don't remember reading any reference to Oberon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T03:02:21-07:00","id":1089673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089082#post1089082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would be weird.<br /> <br /> Too much of a Dreaming = Bad<br /> Too much of Dreaming/Wild Magic &gt;&gt;&gt; Nightmare<br /> Too much of a Nightmare &gt;&gt;&gt; Bedlam<br /> Also, Nightmare = Fomorian<br /> <br /> Undoing (Banality) is opposite to Bedlam (Glamour)<br /> <br /> Ergo to fight off Fomorian Dream &gt;&gt;&gt; Embrace Banality(???)<br /> <br /> Banality = Thuathan Dream(???)<br /> <br /> Resisting Banality = defying the will of Thuatha de Dannan(?????)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really interesting.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that the Tuatha d\u00e9 Danaan created the Mists creating the Sundering. Don't forget that they chose the Fading Path, and also (it's my interpretation) the Escheat was strongly influenced by them... and it advocates the Right of Ignorance. I think that the Escheat is a reflection of the oaths that the Kithain swore to the Tuatha d\u00e9 Danaan when they left them to tend for the Earth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T03:09:00-07:00","id":1089674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089201#post1089201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a contrary, most probably some geeky scientist already counted. The problem is to quickly find out who. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Georges Dum\u00e9zil has studied extensively the structures behind the different mythologies. I really recommend reading him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T03:55:57-07:00","id":1089694,"title":"","content":"So what do you think the Fomorians and Tuatha are actually doing in their homeland, besides maybe plotting to take over the Earth...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T04:09:44-07:00","id":1089700,"title":"","content":"One time I had this weird idea, that there are no Fomorian and Tuatha anymore. That Kithain, Gallain and Thallain <b><i>were</i></b> the Tuatha and Fomorians once before. But, now it's all that is left of the Eldritch Gods and Stewards of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> More on topic, I haven't even the slightest clue. Tuathan departure makes no sense to me.They might as well leave into the alternate universe to start the Scion setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-08-2017, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T04:47:30-07:00","id":1089704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089054#post1089054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it was Lords of Nightmare. There is a Facebook group for it still. A few of us tried to revive it a year or so ago, but things stalled until now. I mainly did a bit of editing on the already-written material. It was really good. Made the Fomorians playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>where can I find it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:00:09-07:00","id":1089710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089704#post1089704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where can I find it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/1096922423673857/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/1096922423673857/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:02:35-07:00","id":1089711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089700#post1089700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One time I had this weird idea, that there are no Fomorian and Tuatha anymore. That Kithain, Gallain and Thallain <b><i>were</i></b> the Tuatha and Fomorians once before. But, now it's all that is left of the Eldritch Gods and Stewards of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> More on topic, I haven't even the slightest clue. Tuathan departure makes no sense to me.They might as well leave into the alternate universe to start the Scion setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I toyed with this idea too, which is quite fascinating, much like in Changeling: the Lost it is hinted that Arcadia *is* our world but only the Mask (or the Mists, if you're in Changeling: the Dreaming) prevents us from seeing it from this perspective. There is no Umbra, no Dreaming; there was no Sundering or Shattering -- or, rather, the Sundering and Shattering were only the divorce between what we want to see and what is here, just beyond our mundane perception, hidden in plain sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:13:27-07:00","id":1089715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089711#post1089711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I toyed with this idea too, which is quite fascinating, much like in Changeling: the Lost it is hinted that Arcadia *is* our world but only the Mask (or the Mists, if you're in Changeling: the Dreaming) prevents us from seeing it from this perspective. There is no Umbra, no Dreaming; there was no Sundering or Shattering -- or, rather, the Sundering and Shattering were only the divorce between what we want to see and what is here, just beyond our mundane perception, hidden in plain sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me <b>KULT</b> a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:32:28-07:00","id":1089721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089694#post1089694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do you think the Fomorians and Tuatha are actually doing in their homeland, besides maybe plotting to take over the Earth...</div> </div> </div> </div>Striding the land like colossi. Calling down blizzards with a mighty roar. Churning the ocean into gargantuan whirlpools. Haunting the dreams of hundreds of thousands of people simultaneously. Carving mountains using sanity-blasting songs as instruments. Y'know, epic stuff worthy of the architects of the Dreaming and nightmare-gods from the dawn of man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:39:46-07:00","id":1089723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089721#post1089721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Striding the land like colossi. Calling down blizzards with a mighty roar. Churning the ocean into gargantuan whirlpools. Haunting the dreams of hundreds of thousands of people simultaneously. Carving mountains using sanity-blasting songs as instruments. Y'know, epic stuff worthy of the architects of the Dreaming and nightmare-gods from the dawn of man.</div> </div> </div> </div>But uhhh are new gods coming into being? Is the Dagdha any different now then a thousand years ago? And what connection do Tuatha have to say Incarna and Spirits in General?<br /> <br /> What would the Wendigo Tribe think of a Wendigo Changeling, which would probably be a Thallain...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:39:56-07:00","id":1089724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089721#post1089721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Striding the land like colossi. Calling down blizzards with a mighty roar. Churning the ocean into gargantuan whirlpools. Haunting the dreams of hundreds of thousands of people simultaneously. Carving mountains using sanity-blasting songs as instruments. Y'know, epic stuff worthy of the architects of the Dreaming and nightmare-gods from the dawn of man.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has surprisingly low impact on the rest of the World of Darkness. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:41:36-07:00","id":1089725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089724#post1089724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That has surprisingly low impact on the rest of the World of Darkness. =)</div> </div> </div> </div>....which is the whole point. The Dreaming may have immense power in it, but, ultimately, disbelief and indifference are its fatal weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:43:30-07:00","id":1089727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089723#post1089723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But uhhh are new gods coming into being? Is the Dagdha any different now then a thousand years ago? And what connection do Tuatha have to say Incarna and Spirits in General?<br /> <br /> What would the Wendigo Tribe think of a Wendigo Changeling, which would probably be a Thallain...</div> </div> </div> </div>Are new gods coming into being, in the Dreaming? Sure, I don't see why not. Human belief in the divine changes all the time.<br /> <br /> As to Wendigo changelings? I'd make them the Nunnehi equivalent of redcaps, rather than shoehorning them as Thallain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:52:01-07:00","id":1089729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089725#post1089725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....which is the whole point. The Dreaming may have immense power in it, but, ultimately, disbelief and indifference are its fatal weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Tuatha of today are no different from the most powerful of chimeras.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Inconsequential.</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:58:25-07:00","id":1089731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089729#post1089729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then Tuatha of today are no different from the most powerful of chimeras.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Inconsequential.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>.....which is <i>also</i> true. The gods of the Dreaming haven't been a factor in the Waking World in a looooooong time, so, yes, their influence is negligible. If you're looking for a game involving ungodly old monsters being the movers and shakers, Changeling is not the game for you.<br /> <br /> However, the Fomorians <i>are</i> rising; the Adhene <i>are</i> freed; and the Thallain <i>are</i> rallying. The Fomorians are returning, and may well soon go from 'meaningless relic' to 'nightmare overlords of Earth' in surprisingly little time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:01:07-07:00","id":1089735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089727#post1089727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are new gods coming into being, in the Dreaming? Sure, I don't see why not. Human belief in the divine changes all the time.<br /> <br /> As to Wendigo changelings? I'd make them the Nunnehi equivalent of redcaps, rather than shoehorning them as Thallain.</div> </div> </div> </div>But wouldn't it be more accurate to say you'd be shoehorning them as Nunnehi equivalent of Redcaps, rather then making them Thallain... I mean they are spirits of cannibalism, agony, hunger and Winter...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:03:23-07:00","id":1089736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089735#post1089735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wouldn't it be more accurate to say you'd be shoehorning them as Nunnehi equivalent of Redcaps, rather then making them Thallain... I mean they are spirits of cannibalism, agony, hunger and Winter...</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>do</i> have a point. So, I suppose Thallain it is!<br /> <br /> ....even though redcaps are <i>also</i> embodiments of dreams of hunger, cannibalism, agony and winter, and <i>they're</i> not Thallain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:08:44-07:00","id":1089738,"title":"","content":"That is true, but at least Cannibalism and Winter are optional-ish for em. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:16:52-07:00","id":1089741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089731#post1089731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .....which is <i>also</i> true. The gods of the Dreaming haven't been a factor in the Waking World in a looooooong time, so, yes, their influence is negligible. If you're looking for a game involving ungodly old monsters being the movers and shakers, Changeling is not the game for you.<br /> <br /> However, the Fomorians <i>are</i> rising; the Adhene <i>are</i> freed; and the Thallain <i>are</i> rallying. The Fomorians are returning, and may well soon go from 'meaningless relic' to 'nightmare overlords of Earth' in surprisingly little time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two paragraphs contradicting each other, don't you think? Either it is a game involving ungodly old monsters being the movers and shakers or not.<br /> <br /> If Fomorians are capable of wrecking the shit up, there has to be a very good reason, why a) Tuatha don't involve themselves at opposing them and b) didn't exercise their power at all since their victory over Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Either the Tuatha are dead, literally or figuratively and can't do anything about that or they think they have already won - i.e. the current state of the world is the direct result of Tuathan actions/inactions during Fomorians imprisonment and is closely aligned with their agenda. That includes Banality and Shattering.<br /> <br /> Or... I'd like to hear your guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-08-2017, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:42:57-07:00","id":1089749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089741#post1089741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those two paragraphs contradicting each other, don't you think? Either it is a game involving ungodly old monsters being the movers and shakers or not.<br /> <br /> If Fomorians are capable of wrecking the shit up, there has to be a very good reason, why a) Tuatha don't involve themselves at opposing them and b) didn't exercise their power at all since their victory over Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Either the Tuatha are dead, literally or figuratively and can't do anything about that or they think they have already won - i.e. the current state of the world is the direct result of Tuathan actions/inactions during Fomorians imprisonment and is closely aligned with their agenda. That includes Banality and Shattering.<br /> <br /> Or... I'd like to hear your guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tuatha de Danaan canonically chose the Path of Fading. They abandoned Earth. Yes, that's a s**t maneuver. Yes, it's repehensible. Yes, that means Banality and the Shattering were likely something the Tuatha de Danaan foresaw, and did what they did, anyways. No, the Tuatha de Danaan are not coming back. Yes, the Kithain are on their own. No, the Fomorians are not yet the hidden powers-behind-the-throne, but they're gathering their forces in preparation for when they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:37:53-07:00","id":1089808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089338#post1089338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ogdoad were primordial gods, but not antagonistic as far as I know?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the myth, I think. Or the translation of the myths. They're not generally antagonistic, but they're also not Indo-European myths. Proponents of comparative mythology claim the meme of elder gods slain by new gods is a story of Indo-European conquest of native cultures when they settled in new lands. They're specific to those cultures. However, other cultures had different myths which don't have very good analogues, but you could force them, if you wanted the Tuatha and Fomorians to be universal. For my money, that's why the hsien are different: they don't have the same cultural origins. They're animistic and pantheistic instead.<br /> <br /> As for the Tuatha . . . Well, C20 actually presents another option. You see, beings who become imbalanced towards Glamour accumulate more Nightmare, which is the realm of the Fomorian Dream. Eventually they enter Bedlam (you used to be able to enter Bedlam without Nightmare, but not so any more). Perhaps the Tuatha, in 'retreating' from humanity, actually entered Bedlam--a state now inextricably tied to Nightmare in the RAW.<br /> <br /> Which means the Tuatha may actually be Fomorians themselves now. Maybe the only difference between Tuatha and Fomorians is their proximity to human dreams--the more you're shaped by the higher thoughts and feelings of humans, the further you move from the chaotic, primal nature of the Fomorians. Once you abandon humanity, you slip back to that earlier, more monstrous state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:44:36-07:00","id":1089813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1089808#post1089808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Tuatha . . . Well, C20 actually presents another option. You see, beings who become imbalanced towards Glamour accumulate more Nightmare, which is the realm of the Fomorian Dream. Eventually they enter Bedlam (you used to be able to enter Bedlam without Nightmare, but not so any more). Perhaps the Tuatha, in 'retreating' from humanity, actually entered Bedlam--a state now inextricably tied to Nightmare in the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could get some answers from a game writer in the other thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jonsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1089376#post1089376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heya! I did some work on the design for Nightmare, Imbalance, and Bedlam in C20. I may be able to offer some perspective on how and why those parts of the game were changed.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jonsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1089425#post1089425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stat and Nightmare dice are distinct from the legacies and realm. From a design perspective, using a term like Nightmare for multiple purposes that don't intersect is a no-no, but there were several points in the design process for C20 were we had to strike a balance between respecting the previous edition and adding/changing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, I like your theory! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T11:09:45-07:00","id":1089861,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I read that explanation too. They should just call Nightmare Dice something else. Wyrd Dice or Wyld Dice would do--in fact, the latter would be far more accurate since these Nightmare Dice have nothing to do with Nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:01:01-07:00","id":1090861,"title":"","content":"Egad! Do we have the Triat invading Changeling now? Banality = Weaver, Bedlam = Wyld, Nightmare = Wyrm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:43:19-07:00","id":1090874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1090861#post1090861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Egad! Do we have the Triat invading Changeling now? Banality = Weaver, Bedlam = Wyld, Nightmare = Wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyld doesn't have to be a reference to the Triat. Spell it Wild Dice, if you prefer. I'm just suggesting something more accurate than Nightmare Dice, since they're explicitly nothing to do with Nightmare any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:43:40-07:00","id":1090920,"title":"","content":"On the subject's title, the mention of \u201cother Pantheons\u201d made me think of <b>Scion</b>. Tuatha/Fomorians are one set of Gods/Titans in that game, and other Pantheons had their own Gods/Titans pairs. Given <b>Changeling</b>'s historical bias toward British Isles mythology among the Kithain, I tend to think that other kinds of Fae would be associated with other Pantheons. In <b>Scion</b> terms, changelings would be Lesser Immortals. And Thallain would be Titanspawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-10-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T02:12:37-07:00","id":1091023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089031-tuatha-fomorians-and-other-pantheons?p=1090920#post1090920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject's title, the mention of \u201cother Pantheons\u201d made me think of <b>Scion</b>. Tuatha/Fomorians are one set of Gods/Titans in that game, and other Pantheons had their own Gods/Titans pairs. Given <b>Changeling</b>'s historical bias toward British Isles mythology among the Kithain, I tend to think that other kinds of Fae would be associated with other Pantheons. In <b>Scion</b> terms, changelings would be Lesser Immortals. And Thallain would be Titanspawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would work. What are the various god/titan pairs in Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T20:10:42-07:00","id":1092639,"title":"","content":"Personally, I make use of mythology books or websites and have included the names of the various elder gods. My players have multicultural character make up and I refer to the Fomorian equivalent for the characters. They are expected to say them in the same manner as well. I also found the comics of Conan and Slaine a while ago. Slaine more than Conan talks about the Irish mythology and they include things for the Norse as well. Both have RPG versions as well that are helpful for ideas. Scion is definitely a good source for at least being a spring board to research for those other pantheons. The works of HP Lovecraft are a standby when I need to get a generic nightmare creature or sometimes they can be expys for anything on the roster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","user":"KyleFianna","date":". 05-14-2017, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T18:27:17-07:00","id":1093931,"title":"","content":"Fomorians have their Courts. <br /> <br /> Why not Tuatha as well have different groups too? <br /> <br /> Why not have groups of Powerful Others, who are neither?<br /> <br /> Some mythologies (and fae families) are born with the help of Dreams and Nightmares duality, others might be fostered by one side or another. Some might be a domain of Others.<br /> <br /> Think Norse Gods: Are Tuatha? Or Chimera? Who are Vanir and how they're different from Aesir?<br /> <br /> There just might be no singular Tuathan or Fomorian Force. Maybe, most gods of the Dreaming just doesn't care. Whoever awakens in the Deep Dreaming to take over the Autumn World, might be just some sore losers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}